WEBVTT

00:05.088 --> 00:06.965
Come out, demon.

00:07.465 --> 00:09.634
Stop!

00:09.718 --> 00:12.595
I have your favorite human blood here!

00:16.766 --> 00:19.728
DESTROY

02:09.129 --> 02:10.880
What's stopping you?

02:10.964 --> 02:12.465
Come closer.

02:12.549 --> 02:14.092
You want it, right?

02:21.975 --> 02:23.309
Mr. Iguro.

02:23.393 --> 02:25.395
You're being too hard on him.

02:25.478 --> 02:27.188
Can you be gentler?

02:27.730 --> 02:30.733
I have to pin him down hard
because he's trying to move.

02:33.194 --> 02:34.612
Tanjiro.

02:34.696 --> 02:38.324
If you use any breathing technique
when your lungs are pressed down,

02:38.408 --> 02:40.076
it will break your blood vessels.

02:40.160 --> 02:41.661
His blood vessels will break?

02:41.744 --> 02:44.330
Great, that would be fantastic!

02:44.414 --> 02:46.332
Come on, break your blood vessels!

02:49.377 --> 02:50.837
I feel pity for him.

02:51.754 --> 02:54.465
He's such a frail, sorrowful child.

02:54.966 --> 02:56.885
Namo Amitabha.

03:10.899 --> 03:12.233
Tanjiro?

03:22.452 --> 03:23.453
Nezuko!

03:35.632 --> 03:37.008
My younger sister.

03:37.091 --> 03:38.384
She's my younger sister!

03:39.093 --> 03:40.428
It wasn't Nezuko!

03:41.054 --> 03:43.598
Although I don't know
why she become like this…

04:07.538 --> 04:10.291
Humans are your family.

04:18.508 --> 04:20.218
You must protect them.

04:28.851 --> 04:32.730
Humans are to be protected and saved.

04:33.314 --> 04:34.399
Not to be harmed.

04:35.775 --> 04:37.568
Never to be harmed.

05:02.552 --> 05:03.845
What happened?

05:04.804 --> 05:07.390
The demon girl is resisting
by turning away.

05:07.890 --> 05:10.810
Although she was stabbed thrice
by Lord Shinazugawa

05:10.893 --> 05:13.521
and even though there's
a bloodied arm in front of her,

05:13.604 --> 05:16.024
the demon girl still refuses to bite him.

05:19.402 --> 05:24.073
So we have sufficient evidence
that Nezuko won't attack humans.

05:29.329 --> 05:31.164
What are you thinking of, Tomioka?

05:32.582 --> 05:33.624
Tanjiro.

05:35.585 --> 05:39.756
Even so, there will be people
who remain suspicious of Nezuko.

05:41.090 --> 05:43.217
You have to back it up with evidence.

05:43.760 --> 05:44.719
From now on,

05:45.428 --> 05:49.098
Tanjiro and Nezuko will fight
and contribute to the cause

05:49.182 --> 05:50.975
as members of the Demon Slayer Corps.

05:54.771 --> 05:56.856
What am I feeling?

05:57.607 --> 05:59.108
I feel as light as a feather.

05:59.817 --> 06:01.235
That voice…

06:01.319 --> 06:05.364
Is it his voice that alleviated my mind?

06:07.075 --> 06:09.410
Your struggle
against the Twelve Demon Moons

06:10.078 --> 06:12.288
has gained our recognition all along.

06:13.081 --> 06:15.958
Your claims
carry a lot of weight, Tanjiro.

06:20.922 --> 06:22.048
I…

06:23.091 --> 06:26.469
Nezuko and I will defeat Muzan Kibutsuji!

06:27.178 --> 06:29.347
I promise that we both will succeed.

06:29.430 --> 06:32.225
We'll cut off the chains of sorrow
with my blade!

06:34.477 --> 06:37.271
That is still far-fetched
given your present status.

06:37.355 --> 06:40.191
Perhaps you can say that
after defeating one Demon Moon.

06:41.734 --> 06:42.819
Yes, sir.

06:44.028 --> 06:45.446
I must keep myself from laughing.

06:45.530 --> 06:46.697
But I can't!

06:47.240 --> 06:49.450
The Hashiras of the Demon Slayer Corps

06:49.534 --> 06:52.203
have outstanding talents,
to say the least.

06:53.162 --> 06:57.875
They have poured blood, sweat, and tears
to prepare themselves for the worst

06:57.959 --> 07:00.378
so that they can vanquish
the Twelve Demon Moons.

07:01.379 --> 07:02.797
Remember this, okay?

07:03.381 --> 07:08.094
That is how the Hashiras
gained respect and deference.

07:08.177 --> 07:11.556
Tanjiro, you must also learn
to mind your words.

07:13.349 --> 07:14.308
Yes, sir.

07:15.935 --> 07:18.020
With that said, Sanemi,

07:18.521 --> 07:19.605
Obanai,

07:20.440 --> 07:23.276
you should not be too harsh on that boy.

07:24.235 --> 07:25.403
As you wish, sir.

07:28.948 --> 07:30.074
As you wish, sir.

07:31.242 --> 07:33.953
That is all for now in regards to Tanjiro.

07:34.620 --> 07:36.205
You are all dismissed.

07:38.291 --> 07:40.126
May I make a request

07:40.209 --> 07:42.879
that Tanjiro be handed over
to my house for care?

07:47.592 --> 07:49.927
Yes, take them away.

07:55.516 --> 07:57.185
Excuse me, everyone!

08:10.490 --> 08:12.950
So, let us begin the Hashiras' Meet--

08:13.034 --> 08:16.537
-Wait!
-Stop!

08:19.540 --> 08:23.711
Let me headbutt
that guy with a lot of scars.

08:23.794 --> 08:26.547
-I'm totally--
-Shut up, will you?

08:26.631 --> 08:29.884
I'm going to make him pay
for stabbing my sister!

08:29.967 --> 08:33.054
It wouldn't be against the rules
if I just headbutt him, right?

08:33.137 --> 08:35.640
Could you please watch your words?

08:35.723 --> 08:37.308
Let me go!

08:37.391 --> 08:38.392
Shut up!

08:45.149 --> 08:48.444
You should not interrupt
when Lord Oyakata is speaking.

08:49.362 --> 08:51.781
-I'm terribly sorry about this.
-We're terribly sorry,

08:51.864 --> 08:53.449
-Lord Oyakata.
-Lord Tokito.

08:53.533 --> 08:56.118
-We are terribly sorry.
-Please forgive us.

08:56.202 --> 08:57.912
-Muichiro!
-We'll be tough on him.

08:57.995 --> 09:01.249
-That was manly of him to do that.
-Please forgive us.

09:01.832 --> 09:03.209
Back off.

09:03.292 --> 09:04.502
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

09:08.464 --> 09:09.507
Tanjiro.

09:10.383 --> 09:12.301
Send my regards to Ms. Tamayo.

09:17.348 --> 09:18.558
Wait.

09:18.641 --> 09:20.685
I just heard him mention Lady Tamayo.

09:21.811 --> 09:23.813
Shut your crap, okay?

09:23.896 --> 09:25.856
You got us into big trouble.

09:25.940 --> 09:27.567
I almost peed in my pants, you know?

09:28.693 --> 09:30.695
The Hashiras are not
to be messed with, okay?

09:30.778 --> 09:32.613
Didn't you see how solemn they were?

09:32.697 --> 09:34.615
I'll never forgive you for what you did.

09:34.699 --> 09:36.284
Never!

09:36.367 --> 09:39.161
-Now apologize!
-Apologize!

09:40.538 --> 09:42.915
I… I'm sorry.

09:44.959 --> 09:47.003
Hello, is anyone home?

09:49.297 --> 09:51.716
Hello, is anyone home?

09:51.799 --> 09:52.883
Excuse us…

09:54.427 --> 09:56.596
There's no one here.

09:57.930 --> 09:59.932
Let's check out the courtyard.

10:03.477 --> 10:05.146
We should drop you off here.

10:06.105 --> 10:07.690
I'm sorry.

10:07.773 --> 10:10.526
But I'm in so much pain, it's killing me.

10:13.529 --> 10:15.323
The headquarters is quite spacious, but…

10:15.990 --> 10:18.409
this is quite a magnificent place too.

10:21.954 --> 10:25.499
Come to think of it,
this is the Butterfly Estate, isn't it?

10:31.964 --> 10:33.174
Someone is here.

10:34.550 --> 10:35.676
There's someone here.

10:37.011 --> 10:39.639
Well, she is…

10:39.722 --> 10:41.932
Right. She's a successor.

10:42.683 --> 10:44.477
Her name is…

10:44.560 --> 10:45.728
A successor?

10:46.395 --> 10:47.980
Lady Kanao Tsuyuri.

10:55.321 --> 10:57.740
I saw her at the Final Selection.

10:58.866 --> 11:03.704
Don't you remember last night
when she stepped on your foot?

11:05.665 --> 11:09.168
A successor means
she was raised and trained by a Hashira.

11:09.710 --> 11:12.588
She wouldn't have been selected
if not for her amazing talent.

11:13.297 --> 11:15.424
She's pretty extraordinary for a girl.

11:18.260 --> 11:20.304
Sorry for bothering you, Lady Tsuyuri.

11:20.971 --> 11:23.099
We are here under Lady Kocho's orders.

11:24.683 --> 11:26.852
May we enter your quarters, please?

11:32.650 --> 11:34.860
May we enter…

11:40.282 --> 11:41.909
I guess we may.

11:42.827 --> 11:43.911
Who are you?

11:45.037 --> 11:46.497
Well…

11:46.580 --> 11:47.873
Lady Kocho sent us here.

11:48.457 --> 11:50.042
Are you the Kakushi?

11:50.751 --> 11:51.961
You have a patient, right?

11:52.878 --> 11:54.004
Follow me.

11:54.713 --> 11:55.840
Yes.

11:56.674 --> 11:57.675
She's pretty fast.

12:06.350 --> 12:07.601
Five times?

12:07.685 --> 12:10.062
I have to take this five times a day?

12:10.146 --> 12:12.648
Every day for three months?

12:12.731 --> 12:15.359
It's so bad, it's killing my appetite!

12:15.443 --> 12:19.613
The medicine is so bitter
and I'm hurting inside!

12:19.697 --> 12:22.533
Do I have to take this
if I want my limbs to heal?

12:22.616 --> 12:24.410
Really? Can it really heal me?

12:24.493 --> 12:26.287
-Please keep it down.
-Please tell me specifically

12:26.370 --> 12:28.330
how it will heal me.

12:28.414 --> 12:30.207
I demand a good explanation!

12:30.291 --> 12:33.377
-Yet another ruckus from him.
-How will one dose heal me?

12:33.461 --> 12:36.130
How will it heal my arms and legs?

12:36.213 --> 12:38.257
-What will happen to them?
-Zenitsu.

12:38.340 --> 12:40.509
-Tell me!
-Can you please be quiet?

12:40.593 --> 12:42.219
Please!

12:42.303 --> 12:44.763
I've explained it to you countless times.

12:44.847 --> 12:47.308
If you don't do what you have to do,
I'll tie you to the bed.

12:50.102 --> 12:51.687
I can't stand you.

12:53.856 --> 12:54.857
Zenitsu.

12:56.275 --> 12:58.402
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

12:59.153 --> 13:01.197
You went up the mountain, didn't you?

13:03.574 --> 13:04.867
Tanjiro?

13:06.952 --> 13:08.871
Tanjiro!

13:08.954 --> 13:10.956
Listen to me!

13:11.040 --> 13:12.750
That stinking spider stung me so badly,

13:12.833 --> 13:15.920
its venom was killing me in agony!

13:16.003 --> 13:19.423
And then, that girl kept berating me.

13:19.507 --> 13:20.883
-I can't take it anymore!
-Goodness.

13:20.966 --> 13:23.135
Let me go. I have nothing to do with this.

13:25.095 --> 13:28.098
Zenitsu, you seem to have shrunk.

13:30.809 --> 13:33.145
Because I almost turned into a spider.

13:33.229 --> 13:36.273
That's why my arms and legs are shorter.

13:36.357 --> 13:37.566
I see.

13:38.317 --> 13:39.610
Where's Inosuke?

13:39.693 --> 13:41.403
Did you see Mr. Murata?

13:41.987 --> 13:46.867
I don't remember Mr. Murata,
but Inosuke is right next to me.

13:48.285 --> 13:49.411
I see him.

13:50.329 --> 13:51.956
He's right there.

13:52.039 --> 13:53.415
I didn't notice him at all.

13:56.961 --> 13:58.087
Inosuke,

13:58.170 --> 13:59.588
I'm glad you're all right.

14:01.882 --> 14:03.551
I'm glad you're all right.

14:04.301 --> 14:07.179
I'm so sorry. I couldn't save you.

14:09.682 --> 14:11.350
It's okay.

14:11.433 --> 14:12.893
Don't worry about it.

14:13.686 --> 14:14.770
Tissues, please!

14:14.853 --> 14:18.774
-That voice… Is it really Inosuke?
-How do you wipe this off of me?

14:19.775 --> 14:22.486
Looks like his voice broke.

14:24.405 --> 14:27.074
I don't know what happened in detail,

14:27.157 --> 14:30.119
but someone choked him hard on the neck.

14:30.202 --> 14:34.290
In the end, he screamed so hard
that it almost killed him.

14:34.373 --> 14:36.166
So his voice box is severely damaged.

14:36.250 --> 14:40.921
Maybe he has turned soft because
he was depressed, but it's so funny.

14:44.174 --> 14:46.969
I wonder why it grosses me out
when I see you laughing.

14:48.012 --> 14:48.971
Are you okay?

14:52.474 --> 14:53.893
Sorry, guys.

14:53.976 --> 14:55.436
I was too weak.

15:00.858 --> 15:02.443
Cheer up, Inosuke.

15:02.526 --> 15:04.528
You shouldn't be so gloomy.

15:04.612 --> 15:06.614
You did your best back there.

15:06.697 --> 15:07.948
You were amazing.

15:08.032 --> 15:10.659
I'm glad to see you alive and well.

15:11.785 --> 15:13.370
Did I take my morning dose?

15:13.454 --> 15:15.664
Did anyone see me take it? Anyone?

15:15.748 --> 15:18.417
No one saw me?

15:30.971 --> 15:32.139
Zenitsu.

15:32.640 --> 15:33.641
Inosuke.

15:35.309 --> 15:38.103
I'm so happy to see you alive.

16:00.042 --> 16:01.418
You can come out now.

16:02.127 --> 16:04.964
They said you can use this room, Nezuko.

16:08.509 --> 16:10.386
It hurts…

16:13.305 --> 16:16.642
At Natagumo Mountain,
I got beat up so badly.

16:18.102 --> 16:19.603
It hurts so bad.

16:20.104 --> 16:22.439
To be honest, it was agonizing.

16:24.149 --> 16:25.234
Nezuko.

16:26.610 --> 16:29.488
Thank you for protecting me there.

16:31.824 --> 16:33.993
Not only you, Nezuko,

16:34.076 --> 16:36.829
but also Master Urokodaki and Mr. Tomioka

16:37.913 --> 16:41.667
for risking their lives to save us.

16:43.168 --> 16:45.129
Everyone has been caring for us.

16:46.797 --> 16:47.756
I…

16:48.841 --> 16:50.759
I have to be stronger.

16:53.887 --> 16:54.972
Even today,

16:55.764 --> 17:00.644
you can say that Lord Oyakata
spared our lives.

17:03.105 --> 17:04.773
His voice…

17:05.774 --> 17:07.818
had an inconceivable intonation.

17:09.194 --> 17:10.988
Just by listening to him…

17:11.613 --> 17:13.282
makes you feel light inside.

17:14.783 --> 17:16.201
What's up with him really?

17:29.381 --> 17:33.302
I see. You haven't had enough sleep.

17:35.846 --> 17:37.973
It's painful and unbearable,

17:38.807 --> 17:40.517
but I have to work harder

17:41.018 --> 17:44.897
because I'll be an adult soon.

17:45.564 --> 17:49.068
Then, I'll grow old and die.

17:50.861 --> 17:54.907
Then, you as a demon
will be left all alone.

17:57.326 --> 18:00.704
Wouldn't you feel lonely, Nezuko?

18:03.582 --> 18:07.669
I promise that I'll have you
turned back into a human.

18:15.219 --> 18:17.679
As everyone has reported,

18:17.763 --> 18:20.808
the threat of demons of late
has never been so severe.

18:21.517 --> 18:25.896
It can be said that an unprecedented
threat looms over people's livelihoods.

18:26.855 --> 18:29.733
Looks like the Demon Slayer Corps
could use more members.

18:29.817 --> 18:31.401
What is your opinion on this?

18:32.903 --> 18:35.572
Based on what we gathered
from the Natagumo operation,

18:36.365 --> 18:39.910
the quality of our members
has declined incredibly

18:39.993 --> 18:41.787
to the point
that they aren't fit for battle.

18:42.704 --> 18:45.332
First, the trainers have shown
poor judgment.

18:46.250 --> 18:49.920
They must at least be able to determine
if members are fit for battle.

18:50.712 --> 18:53.715
The brat from earlier seems quite useful.

18:54.466 --> 18:57.052
I could see potential in him
as he gave Shinazugawa

18:57.136 --> 18:58.345
a fantastic headbutt.

19:00.389 --> 19:02.724
If we add more manpower,

19:02.808 --> 19:05.811
it will be harder to run the organization
as a whole.

19:06.687 --> 19:10.524
It's so much different today
than in the past.

19:11.400 --> 19:14.945
Besides those who joined after losing
their loved ones in brutal killings,

19:15.529 --> 19:19.449
as well as generations
of pedigree demon hunters,

19:19.533 --> 19:21.952
it would be cruel to expect members
to produce results

19:22.035 --> 19:28.167
by having the same or better level
of determination and courage.

19:28.250 --> 19:30.002
Having said that,

19:30.085 --> 19:33.755
the boy encountered a Demon Moon
not too long after joining the Corps.

19:33.839 --> 19:35.966
I could sense an immense charisma in him.

19:36.049 --> 19:38.969
For those of us who haven't had a chance
to encounter a Demon Moon,

19:39.052 --> 19:40.512
he's worth our admiration.

19:41.722 --> 19:42.931
You're right.

19:43.765 --> 19:49.313
But since the Lower Moons'
reign of terror knows no bounds,

19:49.396 --> 19:52.649
that means Muzan is nowhere
in the vicinity of Natagumo Mountain.

19:54.026 --> 19:56.069
Just like the incident in Asakusa.

19:56.153 --> 19:58.488
Since he was trying to hide something,

19:58.572 --> 20:02.492
Muzan ingeniously caused a commotion
to avoid our detection.

20:03.827 --> 20:06.079
This has ruffled our feathers quite a bit.

20:08.582 --> 20:13.420
Yet the demons are still
devouring people all over

20:13.503 --> 20:16.173
to strengthen themselves
and extend their life span.

20:17.090 --> 20:19.259
For those who have perished
in their fangs,

20:19.343 --> 20:21.553
there is only one thing we must do.

20:23.138 --> 20:25.807
All the Hashiras who have gathered here,

20:25.891 --> 20:29.519
I believe that you are
the elite descendants

20:29.603 --> 20:32.606
of the First Breath users
from the Feudal era.

20:34.149 --> 20:35.400
Tengen Uzui.

20:36.276 --> 20:37.945
Kyojuro Rengoku.

20:38.779 --> 20:40.280
Shinobu Kocho.

20:40.822 --> 20:42.824
Mitsuri Kanroji.

20:42.908 --> 20:44.701
Muichiro Tokito.

20:45.619 --> 20:47.162
Gyomei Himejima.

20:47.996 --> 20:49.539
Sanemi Shinazugawa.

20:50.374 --> 20:51.667
Obanai Iguro.

20:52.459 --> 20:53.919
Giyu Tomioka.

20:55.504 --> 20:57.464
My young warriors.

20:58.048 --> 21:00.467
I expect you to do your very best.

21:11.103 --> 21:12.646
Muzan Kibutsuji.

21:13.397 --> 21:15.607
I'll defeat you no matter what it takes.

21:17.693 --> 21:20.153
You shall fall into our hands.

22:51.953 --> 22:55.207
I still can't believe that there's a demon
that doesn't attack people.

22:55.290 --> 22:56.875
This is simply miraculous, isn't it?

22:56.958 --> 22:58.085
Speaking of miracles,

22:58.168 --> 23:01.546
we still don't have any clue
of where Muzan Kibutsuji may be.

23:01.630 --> 23:03.423
That would be a miracle
on a millennial scale.

23:04.508 --> 23:07.135
It's nice to hear the exaggerations
only you can make.

23:07.219 --> 23:09.930
Here's a little gossip
from the Taisho era.

23:10.013 --> 23:13.683
I believe Lord Oyakata is the 97th leader
of the Demon Slayer Corps.

23:13.767 --> 23:15.477
To seize this golden opportunity,

23:15.560 --> 23:18.814
we, the Hashiras, must give our support
to the Demon Slayer Corps.

23:18.897 --> 23:20.899
Do you understand, Sound Hashira?

23:20.982 --> 23:22.984
I don't need you to remind me,
Flame Hashira.

23:23.068 --> 23:26.696
Next, episode 24,
"Rehabilitation Training."

23:26.780 --> 23:28.365
TO BE CONTINUED

23:28.448 --> 23:30.033
Subtitle translation by CL Tan
